WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:03.800
A movie's success at the box office is no
indication of quality.

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:07.100
Mediocre movies make hundreds of millions
of dollars all the time.

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:11.580
These movies may have drawn crowds on opening
weekend, only to be almost completely forgotten

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:12.960
in the months and years that followed.

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:15.780
Here are the least memorable number one movies
of all time.

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:17.540
The Karate Kid

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:23.140
2010's The Karate Kid is less a remake of
the '80s high school movie classic and more

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:26.040
a reimagining, borrowing the core concepts
of the original film.

00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:30.440
It accentuates the fish-out-of-water element
of the source material by having Jaden Smith's

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:32.820
Dre Parker move from Detroit to China.

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:37.160
There, he meets the enigmatic Mr. Han, who
teaches him the ways of kung fu to help deal

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:38.240
with some school bullies.

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:42.399
It seemed to have all the makings of a hit
and the beginning of a new era for the franchise.

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:45.080
While the former proved to be true, the latter
didn't.

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:49.440
After debuting at Number 1 and making bank
during its box office run, the film never

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:50.950
caught on like the original.

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:54.180
It may come down to substituting simple charm
with elaborate martial arts.

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:58.540
It also doesn't help that the film focuses
on younger kids than the originals did, making

00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:00.300
it far more cringe-inducing at times.

00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:03.560
"I put my jacket on a thousand times.

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:05.760
I took it off A THOUSAND times.

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:06.260
OK?

00:01:06.260 --> 00:01:06.760
This stupid!"

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:12.240
Now that the original franchise has been revived
for TV, the film's long-gestating sequel seems

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:14.720
unlikely to leave development hell anytime
soon.

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:16.400
Tron: Legacy

00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:21.420
Hedging your bets on an expensive sequel to
a long-dormant cult classic seems like a bold

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:25.000
decision, but Disney went for it with 2010's
Tron: Legacy.

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:29.700
The film hit screens nearly 30 years after
its predecessor, and made a solid impression.

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:34.220
Featuring some stunning special effects, bold
sci-fi storytelling, and a great soundtrack

00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:37.640
by Daft Punk, it seemed Tron was back, until
it wasn't.

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:42.189
It seems that awesome special effects and
weird sci-fi storytelling are useless if they

00:01:42.189 --> 00:01:43.960
aren't anchored by compelling characters.

00:01:44.149 --> 00:01:48.460
Sam Flynn, the protagonist played by Garrett
Hedlund, is a bland lead whose every line

00:01:48.460 --> 00:01:52.500
of dialogue seems to be ripped from a list
of the most popular movie phrases of all time.

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:56.180
"You gotta be kidding me."

00:01:56.880 --> 00:02:01.140
All the lightcycle sequences in the world
couldn't get audiences interested in his story.

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:05.960
Plans for a sequel stalled, and aside from
the short-lived animated series Tron: Uprising,

00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:10.100
it looks like Tron: Legacy may be the last
we see of the world of the Grid for some time

00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:11.400
Hancock

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:16.080
The summer of 2008 featured the release of
Iron Man, The Dark Knight, and The Incredible

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:16.580
Hulk.

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:20.660
Throw in a cinematic adaptation of Wanted,
and it's safe to say it was a summer ruled

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:22.140
by comic book adaptations.

00:02:22.360 --> 00:02:25.800
However, there was another superhero movie
that dropped that summer.

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:28.680
We're talking, of course, about the Will Smith
vehicle Hancock.

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:36.420
"What?"

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.360
The film hit number 1 its opening weekend
and went on to become the fourth-highest grossing

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:42.500
movie of 2008.

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:46.020
However, its timing has been its disadvantage
in the long run.

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:50.620
With recognizable name brand superhero movies
coming out every other month these days, projects

00:02:50.629 --> 00:02:53.500
like Hancock have an uphill battle to fight
for attention.

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:58.140
A sequel has since been discussed, but a decade
of Marvel and DC superhero movies dominating

00:02:58.140 --> 00:03:01.000
the box office seems to have put the world
of Hancock on ice.

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:02.480
Tomorrowland

00:03:03.080 --> 00:03:06.640
Films based on Disney theme park attractions
tend to be hit or miss.

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:10.209
On one hand, the Pirates of the Caribbean
franchise is a huge success.

00:03:10.209 --> 00:03:12.840
On the other, the less said about The Country
Bears, the better.

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:22.400
In 2015, it looked like Disney would have
a guaranteed hit with Tomorrowland.

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:26.720
Every facet of the production featured all-stars
in their field, from director Brad Bird and

00:03:26.730 --> 00:03:29.629
writer Damon Lindelof to the film's lead,
George Clooney.

00:03:29.629 --> 00:03:32.769
On its opening weekend, it managed to snag
the number-one spot.

00:03:32.769 --> 00:03:37.060
However, reception was middling at best, with
reviews split almost perfectly down the middle

00:03:37.060 --> 00:03:37.900
on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:43.180
Critics and audiences alike found it uneven,
at times enthralling and exciting and at others

00:03:43.180 --> 00:03:44.700
utterly incomprehensible.

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:48.440
Soon hopes of a new Disney franchise were
halted and the film petered out at the box

00:03:48.440 --> 00:03:48.940
office.

00:03:49.180 --> 00:03:53.460
Despite the high expectations preceding its
arrival, it's proven to be a summer blockbuster

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:55.860
most viewers forgot as soon as they left the
theater.

00:03:56.560 --> 00:03:57.140
Avatar

00:03:57.860 --> 00:04:02.080
When Avatar hit theaters, it mowed down box
office records like an industrial bulldozer.

00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:05.180
"I got a native doing the funky chicken here.

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:06.100
He's blocking my blade."

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:09.240
"Well, keep going, he'll move."

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:14.100
It also garnered critical acclaim, even scoring
a Best Picture nomination at the Oscars.

00:04:14.510 --> 00:04:17.860
It seemed like a movie we'd be talking about
for a very long time.

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:20.220
In a genuinely shocking turn, we didn't.

00:04:20.620 --> 00:04:24.930
Avatar has become perhaps the most notable
instance of a massively popular film fading

00:04:24.930 --> 00:04:25.940
into irrelevance.

00:04:26.180 --> 00:04:29.620
Maybe it's the fact that viewers have since
realized that the film's story is largely

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:30.120
derivative.

00:04:30.340 --> 00:04:34.700
Or maybe the real draw was the film's stunning
3D which makes for a viewing experience that

00:04:34.700 --> 00:04:37.200
can't really be replicated outside a movie
theater.

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:39.320
Ultimately, it's a tough question to answer.

00:04:39.560 --> 00:04:43.460
All we know is that people aren't nearly as
excited about the sequels in development today

00:04:43.460 --> 00:04:45.360
as they might have been in 2010.

00:04:46.040 --> 00:04:47.020
The Incredible Hulk

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:51.610
The Incredible Hulk is a perfectly decent
superhero movie with some great moments.

00:04:51.610 --> 00:04:55.710
Edward Norton is a great choice for Bruce
Banner, and Tim Roth's villainous Abomination

00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:57.640
is, at times, genuinely frightening.

00:04:57.820 --> 00:05:01.570
It also made good money at the box office,
debuting at the top spot over its opening

00:05:01.570 --> 00:05:02.060
weekend.

00:05:02.060 --> 00:05:06.600
Unfortunately it's also a movie that audiences
— and Marvel — have seemed eager to forget.

00:05:06.600 --> 00:05:11.020
The film came out between Iron Man and The
Dark Knight, two absolute game-changers in

00:05:11.020 --> 00:05:13.440
superhero cinema, and it got lost in the shuffle.

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:17.639
Pair this with Norton and Marvel parting ways
and Mark Ruffalo stepping in as Banner, and

00:05:17.640 --> 00:05:20.980
The Incredible Hulk was left on the fringes
of the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:05:21.289 --> 00:05:25.300
The Incredible Hulk now feels like a sort
of relic, the last Marvel film to drop before

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:27.900
the Cinematic Universe Era kicked into high
gear.

00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:31.640
As the MCU sped along, The Incredible Hulk
was left in the dust, and nobody seemed to

00:05:31.640 --> 00:05:32.140
notice.

00:05:32.780 --> 00:05:34.200
The Amazing Spider-Man

00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:39.040
From the first big-screen adaptation of everyone's
favorite web-slinger to the character's first

00:05:39.050 --> 00:05:43.660
MCU movie, Spider-Man: Homecoming, Spidey
movies have never been anything less than

00:05:43.660 --> 00:05:44.840
box office successes.

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:49.720
Marc Webb's The Amazing Spider-Man and The
Amazing Spider-Man 2 were hugely successful,

00:05:49.729 --> 00:05:54.240
well-received critically, and yet completely
failed to make any sort of lasting impression.

00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:58.130
The problem comes down to how transparent
the films are about setting up a big superhero

00:05:58.130 --> 00:06:00.080
franchise to compete with the MCU.

00:06:00.320 --> 00:06:04.419
The Amazing Spider-Man and its sequel may
have been enjoyed by filmgoers at the time,

00:06:04.419 --> 00:06:08.169
but the cold, calculating vibe they give off
caused the audience to lose interest in the

00:06:08.169 --> 00:06:08.669
long run.

00:06:09.169 --> 00:06:13.120
When an opportunity presented itself, Sony
struck a deal with Marvel and scrapped Webb's

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:14.040
planned sequels.

00:06:14.600 --> 00:06:15.800
The Bourne Legacy

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:20.210
The Bourne franchise redefined action movies
for a generation — and did so with Matt

00:06:20.210 --> 00:06:21.220
Damon in the lead.

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:25.280
With the trilogy's story revolving around
his character Jason Bourne, it would seem

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:29.030
ill-advised to make an installment of this
series that doesn't feature him at all.

00:06:29.030 --> 00:06:32.880
That didn't stop the studio from trying in
2012 with The Bourne Legacy.

00:06:32.880 --> 00:06:37.260
The studio brought in Jeremy Renner as Aaron
Cross, a new black ops agent to anchor the

00:06:37.260 --> 00:06:37.760
story.

00:06:37.780 --> 00:06:41.400
It's about as good as a Bourne movie that
doesn't actually feature its title character

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:44.500
could be, but that hasn't really proved to
be enough in the long run.

00:06:44.830 --> 00:06:48.900
Despite debuting in the top spot at the box
office, Renner was such a dud as the series'

00:06:48.900 --> 00:06:52.180
new lead that Damon returned for 2016's Jason
Bourne.

00:06:52.500 --> 00:06:56.440
Now that he's back, we doubt we'll be seeing
a solo Aaron Cross film again any time soon.

00:06:57.020 --> 00:06:58.360
Oz the Great and Powerful

00:06:58.960 --> 00:07:04.160
In 2013, Sam Raimi offered a fresh take on
the lore of Oz with Oz the Great and Powerful.

00:07:04.170 --> 00:07:08.009
The movie boasts an all-star cast that includes
James Franco as the man who would become the

00:07:08.009 --> 00:07:10.840
Wizard of Oz and Mila Kunis as the Wicked
Witch of the West.

00:07:10.970 --> 00:07:14.760
Throw in some stunning special effects and
Raimi's trademark quirk, and you've got a

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:15.860
charming reinvention.

00:07:16.090 --> 00:07:19.620
The film made a decent critical and financial
impression upon release.

00:07:19.629 --> 00:07:23.289
However, the years haven't been particularly
kind to its legacy.

00:07:23.289 --> 00:07:27.919
Despite the stars being signed on for sequels,
Raimi has stated he has no plans to return

00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:29.240
to Oz any time soon.

00:07:29.240 --> 00:07:34.120
And with so many fairytale and fantasy adaptations
hitting screens in the years since, Oz the

00:07:34.129 --> 00:07:36.810
Great and Powerful has become more of a footnote
than a headline.

